        "filename": "Sunken Garden Spring Austin Texas.jpg",
        "caption": "The Sunken Garden Springs in Zilker Park, Austin, Texas, United States. The area was developed by the National Youth Administration in the 1930s. It is off limits today as a sanctuary for the Barton Springs Salamander and the Austin Blind Salamander, both of which are endangered species. The sunken garden is a contributing site to the Zilker Park Historic District which was listed on the National Register of Historic Places on May 23, 1997.",
